The night dark subsides. Outlines of centuries-old trees near you can be seen more clearly; you hear singing of first awaken birds, chirring of insects is coming from the grass. You need to keep moving, today it's necessary to get out of this forest and return home at all costs; overnight stay clearly demonstrated, it`s better not to linger here.
You pack your stuff in a hurry and start marching, trying to stick to some kind of a path, treaded by wild animals. At least there is hope, that it'll lead you to a water source, and then you`ll find the way out.
You have been walking quite for long time, but the forest does not end. Finally, gaps between trees become wider and you come to an edge. You let out an involuntary scream of joy: up ahead, in lowland, you can really discern a vague silhouette of some water body. Firstly you had to reach it, though. The animal trail is leading to another wood, smaller than the forest that you have just passed. The wood consists of short shrubs only. This underbrush is surrounded by fields where high grass grows. Gusts of wind sway plants on the fields; you seem to be so close to the vast lake. It's time to choose, how best to get to water.